From a99e7f81761d7d79a48679e262810c5f9549bf4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: R0rt1z2 <roger@r0rt1z2.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 23:29:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WallpaperManagerService: Never upscale the stored wallpaper

The desired dimensions are square, max(w,h) on both axes, so on a
landscape display the picker's screen-sized bitmap gets blown up here and
shrunk again at draw time. Enlarging adds no detail, so only scale down.

Change-Id: Iaa88cddd447bea80ba9ce33338d88bfc514e9ef1
---
 .../android/server/wallpaper/WallpaperManagerService.java  | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wallpaper/WallpaperManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wallpaper/WallpaperManagerService.java
index ca018dc9..eab5759b 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wallpaper/WallpaperManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wallpaper/WallpaperManagerService.java
@@ -625,8 +625,11 @@ public class WallpaperManagerService extends IWallpaperManager.Stub
                         || options.outWidth > cropHint.width());
             }
 
-            // scale if the crop height winds up not matching the recommended metrics
-            needScale = wpData.mHeight != cropHint.height()
+            // scale if the crop height winds up not matching the recommended metrics.
+            // Only ever scale down: enlarging the source adds no detail, and on displays
+            // whose height is below the recommended (square) size it makes the picker's
+            // screen-sized bitmap get blown up here and shrunk again at draw time.
+            needScale = cropHint.height() > wpData.mHeight
                     || cropHint.height() > GLHelper.getMaxTextureSize()
                     || cropHint.width() > GLHelper.getMaxTextureSize();
 
-- 
